               & " Comments or line breaks retain the observation without "
               & "an automatic edit. The language permits the `mut`; the w"
               & "arning is the compiler's judgement and not a rule (D251)"
               & ". A shared declaration is warned about only when none of"
               & " its names is written, and a module binding never is, si"
               & "nce a linked routine or a debugger may write it. A norma"
               & "l warning does not fail the invocation; `--deny=L0326` e"
               & "xplicitly promotes it to an invocation error.",
            when Catalogue.Call_Argument_Match =>
               "A call's arguments do not match what the callee takes [1"
               & "920]. A runtime argument is missing, extra or given twic"
               & "e; a named argument names no parameter [0980]; a static "
               & "type argument names a value, a function or a field rathe"
               & "r than a type, bare or qualified by its module; a `calle"
               & "r` parameter is filled other than by forwarding another "
               & "one (D186); a static argument is given where the callee "
               & "has no static formal [1300], or a static formal is used "
               & "as a runtime value [1290]; a generic call gives a differ"
               & "ent number of arguments than its template (D138); or a c"
               & "onversion is not given exactly one value [0700]. Supply "
               & "every parameter exactly once, in the callee's declared f"
               & "orm. The second label points to the signature or paramet"
               & "er. When a named argument names no parameter, the diagno"
               & "stic offers the parameter label near it as a likely fix.",
            when Catalogue.Zero_Image_Unavailable =>
               "`zeroed` or an implicit initializer has no complete zero"
               & " image to supply [0540]. `zeroed`, an implicit module in"
               & "itializer, and a module atom binding without an initiali"
               & "zer [0630] each need the destination type's all-bits-zer"
               & "o image. A pointer, function address, atom set without a"
               & " zero identity, a distinct type over one, or aggregate c"
               & "ontaining one has no such image, and `zeroed` nested in "
               & "an expression or used as an operand has no destination t"
               & "o take its type from. A distinct type over a number has "
               & "its base's image, so a record holding one is zeroed, but"
               & " `zeroed` does not construct the identity itself: write "
               & "`name(0)` (D428). Give an explicit initializer that cons"
               & "tructs a valid value, use a type with a zero image, or w"
               & "rite `zeroed` as the whole value of a typed destination."
               & " Thread storage, `link(thread)`, begins zeroed in every "
               & "thread and takes no value (D496), so its type is the one"
               & " to change: keep a pointer in it as a `usize` or as a po"
               & "inter union with an atom, or keep the referenced value i"
               & "tself."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "Two routes cover most programs. An array whose element h"
               & "as no zero image is filled from one valid element, `[n o"
               & "f value]`, rather than zeroed; an array of none has no e"
               & "lement to fill it from, and `[0 of value]` is refused, s"
               & "o it is declared a slice of the element type and given `"
               & "[]`, which holds none. A service's state is declared `ze"
               & "roed` beside the caller's other storage, so it holds onl"
               & "y scalars, and the references the service needs, the bac"
               & "king it was given or the provider it stacks on, live in "
               & "the handle `over` returns from that state (D288): `arena"
               & ".space` holds counters, and the arena's handle holds the"
               & " base.",
            when Catalogue.Error_Contract_Violated =>
               "A failure does not follow the declared error contract [0"
               & "940] [0960] [1030]. `fail` carries exactly one atom of t"
               & "he function's declared error set. A body that can fail w"
               & "ith an atom outside it is told which atom, and the `fail"
               & "`, the call or the `try for` it first came through is la"
               & "belled (D382). A call to a failing function handles the "
               & "outcome with `else` or propagates it with `try`, and nei"
               & "ther form applies to a call that cannot fail. A public o"
               & "r first-class signature writes a concrete error set inst"
               & "ead of `! ...`. Add the atom to the error set, handle or"
               & " propagate the call, or remove the handling from an infa"
               & "llible call. The implicit provider calls in `try for` al"
               & "so propagate their declared errors: the enclosing routin"
               & "e must declare or infer those atoms, and its caller may "
               & "recover them through ordinary call `else`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "In an `if` arm, `else value` after a call is read as the"
               & " `if`'s own `else` [1820], so the call is left unrecover"
               & "ed: write `(f() else 0)`, or bind the error with `else ("
               & "problem)`. A failing call that ends a body with returns "
               & "is the routine's value [1080], and the message says so; "
               & "its result is checked against the returns once the failu"
               & "re is handled (D871). The hosted `main` declares no `!` "
               & "set [1970], so widening one cannot mend a `try` or an un"
               & "handled call there: handle the failure with `else`, or m"
               & "ove the work into a routine whose set holds it and handl"
               & "e that call's failure in `main` (D872).",
            when Catalogue.Assembly_Block_Contract =>
               "An assembly block, operand or template breaks [1630]'s b"
               & "lock contract or [1990]'s register rules. Only `assemble"
               & "r.block` accepts operands. Each operand is one integer r"
               & "egister, named by its target-wide name or chosen with `g"
               & "eneral`, and never a stack, frame, link or reserved regi"
               & "ster. Every `{name}` in the template names one operand. "
               & "A naked body is exactly one block. The text holds instru"
               & "ctions, one a line, with no directive or statement separ"
               & "ator, a label only in a naked body (D598), and a comment"
               & " only in the target's own form: `@` on Cortex-M, `//` on"
               & " arm64, `#` on x86-64 and RV64 (D597). Its numbers are t"
               & "he assembler's and take no digit separator, so `0x1800_0"
               & "000` is written `0x18000000`. Change the operand, regist"
               & "er, template or text as the message says, or move the op"
               & "erands into an assembly block. A pointer crosses as `usi"
               & "ze(p)`, and the routine around the block takes the stora"
               & "ge as `ptr mut u8` or `[]mut u8`, the permission its cal"
               & "lers are checked against (D440).",
            when Catalogue.Result_Use =>
               "A call's result is used in a way its signature does not "
               & "allow. A result that is handed back must be used or disc"
               & "arded with `_ =` [1020], and a call that returns none ha"
               & "s no value to use, infer from, or discard [1920] [1930],"
               & " nor one for its `else` to yield in place of a result [1"
               & "030]: `else none` ignores its failure, and is refused on"
               & " a call that does return a value (D376) unless the call "
               & "is the whole operand of a discard, `_ = f() else none` ("
               & "D406); to use the value, handle the error with `else (pr"
               & "oblem) ... end`. An `if`, `match` or bare `begin` used a"
               & "s a statement takes no value from its branches, so a bra"
               & "nch that ends with one would drop it; in an `if` arm tha"
               & "t value is often a call's `else value` the `if` took as "
               & "its own [1820]. A `noreturn` call never returns at all ["
               & "0890], so it is no value either: it ends the path where "
               & "it stands, and the note says so rather than calling it a"
               & " call that returns none. Destructuring binds the names o"
               & "f a multiple result, each at most once [0990]. Discard t"
               & "he result explicitly, use a call that returns one, or bi"
               & "nd the result names the signature declares.",
            when Catalogue.Control_Value =>
               "A `break` must carry a value exactly when its target nee"
               & "ds one [1180] [1190]; every value-producing fallthrough "
               & "must supply one (D124). Every `break` out of a loop used"
               & " as an expression carries `with`. A finite expression lo"
               & "op leaves through `break with` when it completes. Every "
               & "fallthrough path of a value-producing `if` or block prod"
               & "uces a value; an early return need not. A labelled bare "
               & "block and a statement loop take no value. Add `with` and"
               & " a value to a break from an expression loop. Remove `wit"
               & "h` from a break to a statement loop or labelled bare blo"
               & "ck. Supply a value on each fallthrough path, or use the "
               & "construct as a statement. A value-producing construct mi"
               & "ssing its value on several paths is reported once, again"
               & "st the construct (D263).",
            when Catalogue.Match_Arm_Form =>
               "A `match` arm does not fit its subject [1210]. A subject"
               & " is an atom set, a variant part or a pointer union. Each"
               & " arm names a case or atom of that subject at most once ("
               & "D77) [0640] [0480], and a name twice is L0311. A `ptr` a"
               & "rm matches only a pointer union and binds one read-only "
               & "pointer, or one `sink` pointer that consumes the matched"
               & " place [1220] (D433); no other binding is `sink`. Atom a"
               & "rms bind no payload [0630]. A wildcard arm comes last; o"
               & "n an atom set it may bind one read-only name, `_ (rest):"
               & "`, to the atoms no other arm names, and only when some a"
               & "re left (D434). A variant part takes no wildcard arm: it"
               & "s match names every case, and the refusal names the case"
               & "s the `_` was to cover, to be listed in one arm, `full, "
               & "spare:`, with no missing-case report for each (D866). Va"
               & "riant payload names are positional and complete (D78). R"
               & "ewrite the arm in the form its subject admits, or compar"
               & "e numbers with `if` and `elsif`.",
            when Catalogue.Aggregate_Form =>
               "A struct, variant or array value is built or used outsid"
               & "e its admitted form [0700] [0720]. A construction applie"
               & "s a struct type to labelled field values, and its fill s"
               & "upplies one value for the omitted fields. A variant case"
               & " is written where its part is the destination [0690] (D7"
               & "6). A whole struct or array is copied, passed, returned "
               & "or discarded whole [0670] [0520], and an array is lent w"
               & "hole as the argument of a slice parameter [0570]. A repe"
               & "tition prefix leaves a suffix to fill (D36). Write the v"
               & "alue in the form the note names, at a position that take"
               & "s it. A whole struct passed where a parameter takes some"
               & "thing else is named with its type beside the parameter's"
               & ", and the note names a field of the parameter's type to "
               & "select when the struct has one.",
            when Catalogue.Pointer_Union_Use =>
               "A union of atoms and one pointer is used as a pointer be"
               & "fore it is matched [0480]. Match it first: the `ptr` arm"
               & " binds the pointer, and each atom arm names the empty ca"
               & "se. Asking which case it holds, `m == none_found`, needs"
               & " no match, but two unions do not compare (D429). A point"
               & "er case is constructed only from a pointer, and a known "
               & "zero address is reserved for the union's empty atom [046"
               & "0]. Match the union, or construct it from an atom or a p"
               & "ointer. A C function value is not made from a known zero"
               & " address either, since no code is there [1975]: a lookup"
               & " that finds nothing is a failure to recover from, not a "
               & "function.",
            when Catalogue.Packed_Image =>
               "A packed image or its layout is used outside [0730]'s ru"
               & "les. Packed fields have explicit, disjoint bit positions"
               & " within one unsigned image, and an encoded union has dis"
               & "tinct atoms and encodings. A packed width such as `u2` i"
               & "s a field representation, not an ordinary value type. A "
               & "packed field has no address of its own, cannot be passed"
               & " `inout`, and cannot be sliced; the image is not a scala"
               & "r operand (D228). A field of a `layout(c, packed)` recor"
               & "d, at any depth, has no address of its own either (D410)"
               & ": it is read and written by copy. Correct the layout, or"
               & " work through the containing image or record and its fie"
               & "lds.",
            when Catalogue.Place_Required =>
               "An operation that needs a distinct addressable place was"
               & " given something else. `addr` takes a storage place [043"
               & "0], not a computed value such as a utf8 index result [06"
               & "10]. Two `inout` arguments cannot be one place [0900], a"
               & "nd a `sink` argument is a place rooted in a binding [091"
               & "0]; a match arm's binding is one only when written `ptr "
               & "(sink p)`, and then only over a subject that is such a p"
               & "lace (D433). Store the value in a binding first, or pass"
               & " two different places.",
            when Catalogue.Type_Declaration_Form =>
               "A type position or type declaration is not well formed. "
               & "A type position names a scalar type or a `type` declarat"
               & "ion, and a type name is not a runtime value [1795]. A ty"
               & "pe alias is applied with its exact positional arguments "
               & "[1350]. A union holds atoms and at most one pointer type"
               & " [0640]; a range subtype restricts an integer type [0660"
               & "]; a fixed-array bound is an integer count (D136). Corre"
               & "ct the declaration or name a type.",
            when Catalogue.Signature_Form =>
               "A written signature is not well formed. A function type "
               & "gives each parameter a distinct label [0980] and each re"
               & "sult a distinct name [0990]. A `from` clause names borro"
               & "wed runtime parameters, once each, on a result that hold"
               & "s a reference [0790]. An `escaping into` names another r"
               & "untime parameter whose type holds a reference (D445). A "
               & "`caller` parameter has the exact source-position struct "
               & "(D192). Rename or remove the duplicate, or correct the c"
               & "lause.",
            when Catalogue.Generic_Deduction =>
               "A generic call cannot deduce and instantiate one concret"
               & "e routine (D138). Deduction matches each runtime argumen"
               & "t against its written parameter pattern, an untyped lite"
               & "ral last, when it takes the type its parameter then name"
               & "s (D372); it never uses the return context, conversions "
               & "or constraints, and repeated deductions must agree, and "
               & "the deduced actuals must give a concrete, enabled signat"
               & "ure whose fixed values fit their formals. A generic temp"
               & "late has no function value until it is called. Recursion"
               & " that keeps changing the actual tuple never ends, and a "
               & "circular error-set dependency cannot be resolved (D215)."
               & " Give the type argument explicitly, pass arguments that "
               & "agree, or call a concrete routine.",
            when Catalogue.Conformance_Form =>
               "A concept or conformance declaration is not well formed "
               & "[1230]-[1270]. A concept is parameterized by types and n"
               & "ames each entry once. Composition is finite, and a stati"
               & "c entry name is unique across the concept closure (D221)"
               & ". Every entry fixes one concrete error set. A conformanc"
               & "e names a declared concept, supplies each input and entr"
               & "y once by label, and provides each entry with a function"
               & " of exactly the required signature. A parameterized conf"
               & "ormance applies its complete binder. Correct the declara"
               & "tion against the concept it names. A conformance refused"
               & " for what it lacks is reported once: a use that needs it"
               & " is not refused again for want of one. A parameter or lo"
               & "cal named after a concept hides it [0140], and the diagn"
               & "ostic then names the parameter as the cause (D381). A bi"
               & "nding that holds an anonymous function is a value, not a"
               & " declared function, and supplies no entry; the diagnosti"
               & "c names the binding and says to declare it as a function"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Erased_Contract =>
               "An `any` value or its dispatch is used outside the erase"
               & "d contract [1370] [1380] [1390] (D145-D147). `any C` nam"
               & "es a concept with runtime entries, each dispatch name un"
               & "ique across its closure, and erases a pointer, never a v"
               & "alue; every entry takes the erased `self` first, as a po"
               & "inter or as a record the dispatch copies from that point"
               & "er; an entry is called directly and is not a bound value"
               & "; a concrete pointer selects exactly one conformance, or"
               & " the report names the pointee and every concept it confo"
               & "rms to; and a module `any` binding has no implicit null "
               & "pair. A call through a concept no conformance answers is"
               & " not refused: no value can reach it, and it traps as `un"
               & "reachable` (D377). An entry taking `self: ptr mut` needs"
               & " a mutable address, so a read-only one is refused at the"
               & " address with the receiver that writes beside it [0440]."
               & " Pass a pointer, write the `any C` context, `name: any C"
               & " = any(addr x)` or `name: [N]any C = [...]`, or adjust t"
               & "he concept's entries.",
            when Catalogue.Noreturn_Contract =>
               "A noreturn routine breaks its contract [0890]. A noretur"
               & "n signature is ordinary and infallible, and every reacha"
               & "ble path of its body diverges. Remove the error set, or "
               & "end every path in a call that does not return.",
            when Catalogue.Memory_Contract =>
               "A memory intrinsic is used outside its explicit contract"
               & " [1620] (D227), or a stack builtin outside its own (D450"
               & ", D453). Each operation takes the operand types, permiss"
               & "ions and memory orderings its contract lists, the target"
               & " must support it, and an intrinsic cannot fail. `compile"
               & "r.stack_prepare` takes a `[]mut u8`, an ordinary `(argum"
               & "ent: usize) -> noreturn` entry and a `usize`; `compiler."
               & "stack_switch` takes a `ptr mut usize` and a `usize` (D47"
               & "2); a target whose backend does not emit them yet refuse"
               & "s both by name. Use an ordering and operand the operatio"
               & "n admits on this target. A refusal that names the target"
               & " is made only where the program reaches the call (D564):"
               & " a builtin in an imported routine nothing calls refuses "
               & "nothing, and a module compiled with no `main` reaches ev"
               & "erything it holds."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A pointer the operation does not take is named as the pr"
               & "ogram writes its type. A `core/atomic` cell is not a sca"
               & "lar: it is read and written by its own operations, `atom"
               & "ic.load` and `atomic.store` among them, and the refusal "
               & "of a builtin given one names them."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A `core/atomic` cell the target's atomics cannot carry i"
               & "s refused the same way where the program uses it (D510):"
               & " on every firmware target a `u64` cell, and on Cortex-M,"
               & " Xtensa and RV32 at `rv32imc` a cell's `exchange`, `add`"
               & ", `add_relaxed` and `compare_exchange`. On RV32 the read"
               & "-modify-writes are the level's (D690): build at `rv32ima"
               & "c`, with `--level=rv32imac` or the language server's `le"
               & "vel`, where the core has the A extension. A cell one con"
               & "text alone writes adds with `atomic.sole_add`, a load an"
               & "d a store; state several contexts write takes the target"
               & "'s critical section, in `platform/cortex_m`, `platform/r"
               & "iscv` or `platform/xtensa`.",
            when Catalogue.Machine_Entry_Contract =>
               "An interrupt or naked routine is used outside its machin"
               & "e-entry contract [1570]. An interrupt routine is a firmw"
               & "are target's, and a naked routine a firmware target's or"
               & " one on x86-64, arm64 or RV64; either takes a nongeneric"
               & " `() -> none` signature without errors. A naked body is "
               & "one assembly block. A machine entry is entered by its ve"
               & "ctor and is never called as a routine. Correct the signa"
               & "ture or body, or call an ordinary routine instead.",
            when Catalogue.Foreign_Boundary =>
               "A C boundary declaration or call is something the C ABI "
               & "cannot carry [1580]. RV32 and Xtensa have no C ABI yet, "
               & "so they take no C signature and lay out no `layout(c)` r"
               & "ecord, and the diagnostic names the target; a byte-packe"
               & "d `layout(c, packed)` record needs no C alignment and is"
               & " accepted there. The refusal of a signature names the pa"
               & "rt C cannot carry. Where a C ABI is enabled, a C signatu"
               & "re is infallible and nongeneric, with at most one result"
               & ". Each parameter and result part uses implicit or explic"
               & "it `in`, without `caller` or a constraint. Its type is a"
               & " scalar, pointer (including a named optional pointer uni"
               & "on), fixed infallible C callback, or `layout(c)` struct;"
               & " slices, `any`, atoms and by-value arrays are excluded. "
               & "A `layout(c)` struct has at least one field and holds on"
               & "ly C representations: scalars, pointers, fixed C callbac"
               & "ks, nonempty fixed arrays or recursively `layout(c)` str"
               & "ucts, with no tagged variants; the label names the field"
               & " that is not one. Its last field may be a `[0]T` flexibl"
               & "e array member after at least one other field (D413), an"
               & "d a record ending in one is not a field of another C rec"
               & "ord. A `layout(c, packed)` record holds an array or nest"
               & "ed record by value only when its alignment is one: `u8`,"
               & " `i8`, `bool` or a packed record (D410). A packed record"
               & ", a record with a flexible member, and a record holding "
               & "either cross a C signature only by pointer (D414). A var"
               & "iadic C declaration needs at least one fixed parameter a"
               & "nd target support; a variadic definition needs a generat"
               & "ed adapter. Cortex-M's AAPCS32 calls no variadic C funct"
               & "ion yet (D922): its refusal names the target, and the re"
               & "pair is a C function of fixed arity that makes the varia"
               & "dic call, linked with the program and declared `extern(c"
               & ")` instead. Variadic calls take positional scalar, point"
               & "er or fixed C callback tail arguments, without labels or"
               & " static arguments. Change `inout` or `sink` to `in`; pas"
               & "s a pointer if C must write through a parameter. Remove "
               & "`caller` and constraints, specialize generics, represent"
               & " errors through an ordinary C result, and combine multip"
               & "le results into one C-representable result. Pass a point"
               & "er to a by-value array or other unsupported aggregate, o"
               & "r change the type or layout to one C represents. Pass `p"
               & "tr` to a packed record or one with a flexible member. A "
               & "struct declared without `layout(c)` has Landin's layout "
               & "[0750], which C does not share, so a signature taking or"
               & " returning one by value, or a C record holding one, is r"
               & "efused naming the part and the struct, as in ""C cannot t"
               & "ake `tint`: `color` is not `layout(c)`"", and the repair "
               & "is to declare it `layout(c) struct` (D529).",
            when Catalogue.Linkage_Contract =>
               "A link symbol [1610], hosted initializer [1975], firmwar"
               & "e placement [1640] or thread storage [1996] breaks its c"
               & "ontract. A link symbol denotes one compatible function a"
               & "nd at most one definition. Beside a hosted entry, a decl"
               & "aration carrying `_landin_host_initialize_arguments` is "
               & "exactly `extern(c) (count: i32, values: ptr ptr u8, envi"
               & "ronment: ptr ptr u8) -> none`, which takes C's `argc`, `"
               & "argv` and `envp`. Only the entry module's hosted `main` "
               & "takes the `main` symbol. A datum's link symbol on a host"
               & "ed target has a routine's shape and is never `main`; Cor"
               & "tex data symbols and sections use the spellings, alignme"
               & "nts and vectors [1640] lists. Rename the symbol or corre"
               & "ct the declaration. Two declarations of one C symbol tha"
               & "t differ only in `escaping` are refused too, and the rep"
               & "ort names the parameter: a Landin caller of either is ch"
               & "ecked against what it says, so repeat `escaping` on both"
               & " (D441). A public naked or interrupt routine with no lin"
               & "k name is a global symbol under its own spelling, held t"
               & "o the same rule (D770): to make a C import a naked routi"
               & "ne's view (D516), give the routine the import's `link(sy"
               & "mbol: ...)`. `link(thread)` places a module `mut` bindin"
               & "g that has no value, one instance in every thread (D496)"
               & ": it places no routine, takes no initializer, and takes "
               & "no link symbol or section, which would name or place one"
               & " instance for all of them. Drop the value, make the bind"
               & "ing `mut`, or drop the other attribute.",
            when Catalogue.Traversal_Source =>
               "A `for` source is not something the loop can traverse [1"
               & "150]. A range traversal runs over integers, an array or "
               & "slice is walked by element, and a struct or `any C` sour"
               & "ce selects one exact iterable conformance with one `Cur`"
               & " and `Item` pair (D180). An ordinary pointer is not a `c"
               & "string` (D184). Traverse an integer range or a traversab"
               & "le value, or declare one iterable conformance. Each prov"
               & "ider takes a read-only, non-escaping `ptr T` to the reta"
               & "ined source, with the exact cursor, item, permission and"
               & " origin contract at [1320]; migrate a by-value source pa"
               & "rameter to that pointer contract."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "If the source supplies `fallible_iterable`, use `try for"
               & "` and declare or infer its provider errors in the enclos"
               & "ing routine. That conformance has one exact shared atom "
               & "error set across all four providers. Ordinary `for` only"
               & " selects infallible `iterable`; `try for` prefers `falli"
               & "ble_iterable` when both exist and may use ordinary `iter"
               & "able` when there is no fallible conformance.",
            when Catalogue.Invalid_Description_Directive =>
               "A device description's directive has arguments that are "
               & "not the forms its row in D542 says: the wrong number of "
               & "them, a text where an integer belongs or the reverse, a "
               & "name outside its spelling, a core, boot image kind, plac"
               & "ement or access the compiler does not know, an integer o"
               & "utside the 32-bit address space, a stack that is not a p"
               & "ositive multiple of 8 bytes, or a size given to a placem"
               & "ent other than the stack's. The message says which argum"
               & "ent and the note how the directive is written, such as `"
               & "linker.region(""FLASH"", 0x1000_0000, 2 * 1024 * 1024, ""rx"
               & """)`.",
            when Catalogue.Description_Structure =>
               "A device description is not one module of its own direct"
               & "ives (D542, D543): a description directive stands in a m"
               & "odule that names no device with `compiler.device`, or in"
               & "side a fixed arm, active or not; a description module ho"
               & "lds an import or a declaration other than its directives"
               & "; a description names its device, core, vector table or "
               & "boot image kind twice, or none, names an interrupt or IR"
               & "Q twice, repeats a region's name, or places a part of th"
               & "e image twice or not at all; or the program reaches a se"
               & "cond description. A program is built for one device, and"
               & " selects it by importing its description; write each dir"
               & "ective once, beside `compiler.device`.",
            when Catalogue.Description_Layout =>
               "A device description's parts do not fit together (D543):"
               & " two regions overlap, a placement names a region the des"
               & "cription does not have or one whose access does not fit,"
               & " as code in an `""rw""` region or data in an `""rx""` one, t"
               & "he vector table does not fit its region or would start u"
               & "naligned, an interrupt's slot lies past the vector table"
               & ", the table is longer than the core's architecture allow"
               & "s, or the stack is larger than its region. The message n"
               & "ames the region or the slot.",
            when Catalogue.Description_Core_Mismatch =>
               "A device description's core does not execute what the re"
               & "quest builds (D543): the target is not `cortex-m0`, or `"
               & "--level` is above the core's own, `armv6-m` for `cortex-"
               & "m0` and `cortex-m0plus`, `armv7-m` for `cortex-m3`, `arm"
               & "v7e-m` for `cortex-m4` and `cortex-m7`, and `armv8-m.mai"
               & "n` for `cortex-m33`. A lower M-profile level is accepted"
               & ": a `cortex-m4` builds at `armv7-m` or `armv6-m` too, an"
               & "d a `cortex-m33` at `armv7-m` or `armv6-m`, though not a"
               & "t `armv7e-m`, whose DSP instructions its core may lack; "
               & "a description with a float unit builds at its unit's lev"
               & "el alone (L0546). Build with the target and a level the "
               & "note names. The constrained reference profile, which app"
               & "lies when no description is imported, is the one descrip"
               & "tion used at every level.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Kind_Reserved =>
               "Retired. A device description selected `esp-app-image`, "
               & "a boot image kind refine reserved and did not build (D54"
               & "5). D683 builds it, so nothing raises this.",
            when Catalogue.Region_Placement =>
               "A `link(region: ""NAME"")` placement cannot be met (D547):"
               & " the selected description has no region of that name, th"
               & "e declaration also names its section, which a region pla"
               & "cement chooses itself, or the region's access does not h"
               & "old it: a routine needs a region code runs in, and a mut"
               & "able datum a writable one. On a hosted target placement "
               & "is refused as L0347 is.",
            when Catalogue.No_Description =>
               "A firmware request, a vector placement or a region place"
               & "ment needs a device profile, and none can be selected (D"
               & "543): the program imports no description, and the librar"
               & "y refine found holds no `platform/cortex_m/reference`, o"
               & "r no library was found. Import the device's description,"
               & " or name a library that holds the reference with `--libr"
               & "ary=DIR`.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Form =>
               "A `link(boot_stage)` marks something other than a device"
               & " description's second-stage boot routine (D587): a modul"
               & "e binding, an ordinary routine or an interrupt handler, "
               & "or a naked routine that also names a section, symbol, re"
               & "gion, vector, alignment, `keep` or `thread`. A boot stag"
               & "e is `link(boot_stage) extern(naked) NAME: () -> none`, "
               & "whose body is the one `assembler.block` the boot ROM ent"
               & "ers, and the boot kind alone says where it goes. Write t"
               & "he attribute alone on such a routine, or remove it.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Outside =>
               "A `link(boot_stage)` routine is outside the device descr"
               & "iption the program selects, or the program imports none "
               & "and is given the constrained reference (D587). The secon"
               & "d stage is the device's, as its boot kind is, so it is d"
               & "eclared in the description's own module, beside `compile"
               & "r.boot`. Move it into the description's directory.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Unwanted =>
               "A device description holds a stage, and its boot kind ru"
               & "ns none (D587, D653): an `rp2350-image-block` image begi"
               & "ns with the vector table, which the boot ROM finds throu"
               & "gh the image block, and runs nothing of the description'"
               & "s before reset. An `rp2040-boot2` image begins with a se"
               & "cond stage, and a `vector-table` image may run one from "
               & "its reset vector before reset. Remove the routine, or se"
               & "lect the boot kind that runs it.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Repeated =>
               "A device description holds a second `link(boot_stage)` r"
               & "outine (D587). The boot kind's slot holds one stage, whi"
               & "ch the boot ROM enters at its first byte. The message na"
               & "mes the first; remove one of them.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Missing =>
               "A device description selects `rp2040-boot2`, whose image"
               & " begins with a second stage, and holds no `link(boot_sta"
               & "ge)` routine (D587). Without one the slot would hold no "
               & "code, and the boot ROM would refuse its checksum and sta"
               & "y in its USB boot mode. Add the stage to the description"
               & " as a `link(boot_stage) extern(naked)` routine of at mos"
               & "t 252 bytes once assembled, literals included; `devices/"
               & "descriptions/rp2040/boot2.ldn` in the repository is a po"
               & "rt of pico-sdk's generic one.",
            when Catalogue.Float_Unit_Unsupported =>
               "A device description names a float unit refine does not "
               & "build, or one its core cannot have (D615). A float unit "
               & "is a fact of the core a chip was built with, written in "
               & "the description's hand-written half as `compiler.float_u"
               & "nit(""NAME"")`, and refine builds one: `fpv5-d16`, the Cor"
               & "tex-M7's single- and double-precision FPv5 with sixteen "
               & "double registers, on a `cortex-m7`. The note says which "
               & "unit the description's core may have. Write `compiler.fl"
               & "oat_unit(""fpv5-d16"")` in a Cortex-M7's description, or l"
               & "eave the directive out: a core with no float unit comput"
               & "es in software, as every other core refine builds for do"
               & "es.",
            when Catalogue.Float_Unit_Level =>
               "A device description has a float unit, and the request b"
               & "uilds it at a level whose architecture lacks that unit ("
               & "D615). A float unit changes the C ABI, single- and doubl"
               & "e-precision values travel in its registers, so code buil"
               & "t for the description assumes the unit, and the level th"
               & "at holds `fpv5-d16` is `armv7e-m`. Build with the level "
               & "the note names; a lower level of the same core is accept"
               & "ed only for a description with no float unit.",
            when Catalogue.Cache_Unsupported =>
               "A device description names a cache refine does not build"
               & ", or one its core cannot have (D971). A cache is a fact "
               & "of the core a chip was built with, written in the descri"
               & "ption's hand-written half as `compiler.cache(""KIND"", LIN"
               & "E)`, and refine builds one kind: `armv7-m-l1`, Armv7-M's"
               & " level 1 instruction and data caches with the maintenanc"
               & "e operations of the System Control Block, which among th"
               & "e cores refine builds for only a `cortex-m7` has. A desc"
               & "ription that declares it is a cached profile: reset enab"
               & "les the caches and the entry's return disables them (D97"
               & "3), and `platform/cortex_m` declares its maintenance pro"
               & "vider there. Write `compiler.cache(""armv7-m-l1"", 32)` in"
               & " a Cortex-M7's description, or leave the directive out f"
               & "or a cacheless profile, whose DMA buffers need no mainte"
               & "nance.",
            when Catalogue.Cache_Line_Wrong =>
               "A device description's cache names a line that is not it"
               & "s core's (D971). The line is the unit every maintained r"
               & "ange is a whole number of, and `core/cache` refuses a ra"
               & "nge that is not, so a description that said another woul"
               & "d let a program align its DMA buffers to lines the hardw"
               & "are does not have. A Cortex-M7's `armv7-m-l1` lines are "
               & "32 bytes, as its CCSIDR says for both caches; write `com"
               & "piler.cache(""armv7-m-l1"", 32)`.",
            when Catalogue.Reset_Stage_Return =>
               "A `vector-table` description's stage does not branch to "
               & "compiler-owned reset (D653). The reset vector enters the"
               & " stage before reset has copied the initialized data or c"
               & "leared the zeroed, and the stage ends by entering reset,"
               & " `_landin_firmware_reset`, which it names: nothing else "
               & "runs reset, and a stage that falls off its end traps. Fi"
               & "nish it with `ldr r0, =_landin_firmware_reset` and `bx r"
               & "0`, which reach reset from anywhere in flash. On `rv32` "
               & "the image's entry word enters the stage of an `esp-app-i"
               & "mage` or `vector-table` description (D684), and the stag"
               & "e ends with `j _landin_firmware_reset`.",
            when Catalogue.Reset_Stage_Stack =>
               "A `vector-table` description's stage uses the stack (D65"
               & "3). The stage runs before compiler-owned reset, on the s"
               & "tack pointer the core loaded from the vector table, and "
               & "before any memory may be written: a chip such as the STM"
               & "32H753 permits no write to its RAM until its supply is c"
               & "onfigured. The message names the word that reaches the s"
               & "tack, `push`, `pop`, `sp`, `r13`, `msp` or `psp`; on `rv"
               & "32`, where reset has not yet set the stack pointer when "
               & "the entry word enters the stage (D684), `sp`, `x2` or a "
               & "compressed instruction that addresses through it, `lwsp`"
               & ", `swsp`, `addi16sp` or `addi4spn`. Keep what the stage "
               & "needs in registers. Xtensa entry prepares its window sta"
               & "te, vectors and internal DRAM spill stack before its dev"
               & "ice stage; that architecture's stage may use the prepare"
               & "d stack for windowed ROM calls, while static storage rem"
               & "ains uninitialized.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Kind_Family =>
               "A device description selects a boot image kind its core'"
               & "s family does not boot (D681). An `rp2040-boot2` image b"
               & "egins with a second stage of Thumb code that RP2040's bo"
               & "ot ROM enters, so it is an Arm core's; an `esp-app-image"
               & "` is what an ESP32-C3's or ESP32-C5's ROM loads, so it i"
               & "s a RISC-V core's. `vector-table` and `rp2350-image-bloc"
               & "k` serve both families. Write the kind the core's boot R"
               & "OM reads.",
            when Catalogue.ESP_Image_Facts =>
               "A device description's boot kind and its ESP chip facts "
               & "disagree (D683). An `esp-app-image` names the chip it is"
               & " for and the revisions it runs on, which the ESP32's ROM"
               & " checks before it loads the image, and where in flash th"
               & "e ROM reads it: a description that selects the kind writ"
               & "es `compiler.esp_image(chip, min_revision, max_revision,"
               & " flash_offset)` beside `compiler.boot`, with the chip id"
               & " ESP-IDF's `esp_chip_id_t` gives, the revisions as major"
               & " * 100 + minor, and the offset as a multiple of 4096. A "
               & "description with another boot kind has no use for the di"
               & "rective. Add the facts the chip's technical reference ma"
               & "nual gives, or remove the directive.",
            when Catalogue.RAM_Code_Unplaceable =>
               "A routine placed in RAM, `link(section: "".ramtext.NAME"")"
               & "`, has nowhere to run (D688). Reset copies RAM code into"
               & " the description's data region, so that region must be o"
               & "ne code runs in, `""rwx""`; an `esp-app-image` places its "
               & "RAM code with its text instead, which the ROM already lo"
               & "aded into RAM. A data region that is `""rw""`, as the ESP3"
               & "2-C3's data-bus alias of its SRAM is, would hold bytes t"
               & "he core cannot fetch, and the first call would fault. Pl"
               & "ace the routine in `.text`, or in an executable region o"
               & "f the description with `link(region: ""NAME"")`. The libra"
               & "ry's Xtensa reference, used when a program imports no de"
               & "scription, has such a data region:",
            when Catalogue.Unused_Pure_Local =>
               "An immutable local that is never used and is initialized"
               & " by a direct scalar literal, including a negated integer"
               & " or float literal, can be removed without changing the p"
               & "rogram's meaning (D251). The warning offers that removal"
               & " as an exact fix when the declaration occupies its own l"
               & "ine without comments or attached documentation. Otherwis"
               & "e it reports the observation without an edit. Shared dec"
               & "larations, module bindings and declarations whose initia"
               & "lizer may perform work are not warned about. `--allow=L0"
               & "349` suppresses this observation; `--deny=L0349` enables"
               & " it as an invocation error before emission.",
            when Catalogue.Literal_Rounded_Away =>
               "A float literal converted to an integer, `u64(1.0e18)`, "
               & "has no type of its own, so it is an `f32` [0210], and th"
               & "e conversion truncates the `f32` (D171). Where that roun"
               & "ding changes the integer the conversion gives, or whethe"
               & "r it gives one, the conversion is refused (D760): `u64(1"
               & ".0e18)` would be 999999984306749440. The report names bo"
               & "th integers. Write `f64(...)` around the literal to conv"
               & "ert its `f64` value, or `f32(...)` to keep the rounding "
               & "on purpose. A literal whose rounding gives the same inte"
               & "ger, as `i64(45.7)` does, is converted as written.",
            when Catalogue.Unvalidated_Text_Checked =>
               "`compiler.utf8_unvalidated(bytes)` makes text of bytes w"
               & "ithout reading them (D949), so it is admitted only where"
               & " the program says it answers for them: inside `unchecked"
               & " begin ... end unchecked`. Bytes that are not UTF-8 then"
               & " go unnoticed, and what reads them as text reads them wr"
               & "ongly. Where the bytes come from input, convert them wit"
               & "h `utf8(bytes)`, which traps on malformed bytes, or `tex"
               & "t.from_bytes`, which reports `invalid_text`. Where they "
               & "are valid by construction, because the program has just "
               & "checked them or wrote only whole scalars, put the call i"
               & "n an `unchecked` region.",
            when Catalogue.No_Toolchain =>
               "The requested output cannot be made with the selected ta"
               & "rget, settings or available toolchain [1550]. The diagno"
               & "stic and its note say which of these is the cause. The t"
               & "arget has no backend, has one that emits nothing yet, or"
               & " lacks the requested source debug mode. No toolchain is "
               & "selected, no driver the target names can be started, or,"
               & " on Darwin, the tool that packages debug information can"
               & "not be run. A static Linux link cannot be made: no libra"
               & "ry holding `platform/linux` was found, the program asks "
               & "for `linker.library`, `linker.directory` or `-L` (D524),"
               & " or it refers to C symbols nothing in it defines, each n"
               & "amed with the routine that refers to it, as `platform/po"
               & "six`'s loader refers to `dlopen`; `refine check` reports"
               & " the last two as a compilation would."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "A firmware link takes `linker.library`, `linker.director"
               & "y` and `-L` as a hosted link does, each library a static"
               & " archive `libNAME.a` (D923), so none of them raises this"
               & " code there."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "On Linux the message lists every driver looked for, the "
               & "target's own GCC and the names Debian, Ubuntu and Fedora"
               & " give it, and the note says which package to install, th"
               & "rough `nix-shell -p gcc` on Nix (D364), and that `refine"
               & " check`, `fmt` and `lsp`, and `compile --emit=asm` or `-"
               & "-emit=ir`, need no C driver (D384). The program's own re"
               & "fusals come first, so a static link that meets an undefi"
               & "ned C symbol is refused for that before anything asks fo"
               & "r a driver. Choose a target with a backend, change the d"
               & "ebug mode, link with `--link=libc`, or select or install"
               & " a toolchain as the note directs. `--toolchain=` only he"
               & "lps when a toolchain is absent or unavailable.",
            when Catalogue.Toolchain_Failed =>
               "Executable emission failed [1550]. The assembler or link"
               & "er may have refused the emitted code, or the requested o"
               & "utput could not be produced, verified, or restored. The "
               & "note describes the failure, names paths needed for recov"
               & "ery, and includes tool output when available. refine sta"
               & "rts no tool while `SIGCHLD` is ignored or `SA_NOCLDWAIT`"
               & " is set, since either discards the tool's exit status; i"
               & "t leaves the inherited setting as it is, and the message"
               & " gives the fix before any path. Start refine with `SIGCH"
               & "LD` at its default disposition and `SA_NOCLDWAIT` clear.",
            when Catalogue.Entry_Point_Missing =>
               "`--emit=exe` needs an entry: a hosted `main` of the one "
               & "shape [1970] in the entry module, or the firmware routin"
               & "e `--firmware-entry=` names. A `public main` in a hosted"
               & " program's entry module that is not of that shape is ref"
               & "used when the program is checked or emitted as assembly "
               & "too, where the linker would otherwise find no `main` (D4"
               & "43); a C-convention `main` is [1650]'s own form.",
            when Catalogue.Argument_Not_In_A_Register =>
               "Retired. An internal call could only pass arguments in r"
               & "egisters. The internal calling convention now places eve"
               & "ry argument after the sixth on the stack, so nothing rai"
               & "ses this.",
            when Catalogue.Frame_Not_Addressable =>
               "A verified frame is larger than the target's backend can"
               & " address: the signed 32-bit offsets of x86-64, arm64, RI"
               & "SC-V and Xtensa, or the 32-bit address space on Cortex-M"
               & ". The message names the routine and the limit. Move the "
               & "large local storage into a module value or an allocation"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Image_Budget_Exceeded =>
               "The program's static images exceed the image budget, whi"
               & "ch every target checks before anything is emitted (D537)"
               & ". The budget counts every image the compilation lowers, "
               & "before section garbage collection, because the assembler"
               & " is given every one: what a program's public `main` reac"
               & "hes, and every module value of a firmware image or an ob"
               & "ject. A firmware image is held to its profile: its writt"
               & "en images to the profile's flash and its mutable ones to"
               & " its RAM, 32 KiB and 16 KiB in the constrained reference"
               & " profile. Any other image is held to how far the target "
               & "addresses static data: 2 GiB under x86-64's small code m"
               & "odel, Darwin's static image and RV64's AUIPC, 4 GiB unde"
               & "r arm64's ADRP, and the 32-bit address space on Cortex-M"
               & ". Zero images, which take no object bytes, are held only"
               & " to the address space. The message gives what the images"
               & " take, the part of the budget they exceed and what sets "
               & "it. Make the static data smaller, or allocate it when th"
               & "e program runs; a value that is zero until the program w"
               & "rites it reserves its bytes rather than writing them.",
            when Catalogue.Panic_Contract_Invalid =>
               "The panic handler is invalid, or the program has more ch"
               & "eck sites than their identifier space holds [1670]. Decl"
               & "are the entry module's `panic_handler` public, ordinary,"
               & " nongeneric and infallible, of type `(core/panic.panic_k"
               & "ind, u32) -> noreturn` as the message gives it; for the "
               & "site space, compile less source, since every source byte"
               & " takes one of its 32-bit identifiers for each panic kind"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Firmware_Frame_Exceeds_Stack =>
               "One routine's saved registers and local frame exceed the"
               & " firmware profile's stack [1990], which the description'"
               & "s `linker.place(""stack"", ...)` sets: 4 KiB in each refer"
               & "ence profile. The message gives the size. Move large loc"
               & "al storage elsewhere or make it smaller, or give the sta"
               & "ck more of the device's RAM. This check does not bound c"
               & "alls or interrupt nesting.",
            when Catalogue.Handler_Exceeds_Stack_Margin =>
               "A program that prepares a stack selects a panic handler "
               & "that does not fit the target's stack margin [1670]. A fa"
               & "iled check enters the handler on the stack that overflow"
               & "ed, so the handler and everything it calls run in the ma"
               & "rgin a prepared stack keeps above its base (D472): 640 b"
               & "ytes on x86-64 and arm64, 768 on RV64 and RV32, 1024 on "
               & "Xtensa, and on Cortex-M 384, or 528 with a float unit. T"
               & "he message gives what the handler needs, the margin and "
               & "the target: what the margin pays before the handler, and"
               & " the handler's depth from the stack report's `trap` figu"
               & "re, by its deepest path. When the handler's calls reach "
               & "a foreign call, recursion, a runtime helper or assembly "
               & "that moves the stack, its depth cannot be known, and the"
               & " message names the opening's kind and points at it; a ca"
               & "ll through `any`, a generic's table or a function value "
               & "counts the deepest routine of the program it can reach ("
               & "D570), and opens the graph only when there is none. Make"
               & " the handler's frame smaller, call less from it, or call"
               & " through nothing that opens its graph; a handler that on"
               & "ly records the kind and switches away fits on every targ"
               & "et. A program with no `compiler.stack_prepare`, and one "
               & "that selects no handler, is not refused: the default rep"
               & "ort always fits. The rule is decided from the frames the"
               & " backend emits at the profile being compiled (D474); `re"
               & "fine check` emits them in memory at its own profile, `no"
               & "ne` unless `--optimize` says otherwise, and `refine lsp`"
               & " at `none`, so both refuse what compiling at that profil"
               & "e refuses (D572).",
            when Catalogue.Library_Not_Found =>
               "A link failed, and a library a `linker.library` directiv"
               & "e asks for is in no directory the link searched (D525): "
               & "not in a directory `-L` or `linker.directory` names, as "
               & "`libNAME.so` or `libNAME.a` (on Darwin `libNAME.tbd`, `l"
               & "ibNAME.dylib` or `libNAME.a`), and not where the C drive"
               & "r's `-print-file-name` finds its own. The message names "
               & "the library at its directive, every named directory with"
               & " where it was named, and says that the driver's own dire"
               & "ctories were searched as well. refine looks only after a"
               & " link has failed; a failed link whose libraries are all "
               & "found stays L0501 with the linker's own text. Name the d"
               & "irectory that holds the library with `linker.directory("""
               & "DIR"")`, relative to the declaring file, or with `-L DIR`"
               & " when building, or install the library where the C drive"
               & "r finds it.",
            when Catalogue.Linker_Script_Contract =>
               "A firmware image linked with `--linker-script=FILE`, or "
               & "any RAM-layout firmware image, breaks its checked layout"
               & " contract (D546, D900). The message names the clause: th"
               & "e vector table at the description's boot address with it"
               & "s whole length, a `_landin_firmware_*` startup symbol mi"
               & "ssing, the stack outside a writable region of the descri"
               & "ption or of another size, or an initialized image whose "
               & "load address is not in the region text is placed in. A d"
               & "escription-owned initialization stage is the reset-vecto"
               & "r entry when present. In RAM layout, loaded sections mus"
               & "t be in SRAM, their load and runtime addresses equal, an"
               & "d their ranges clear of the reserved stack. Change the s"
               & "cript so the clause holds; the derived script refine wri"
               & "tes beside the image as `OUT.ld` meets every clause.",
            when Catalogue.Boot_Stage_Object =>
               "The assembled second stage cannot be sealed with the boo"
               & "t ROM's checksum (D588). refine reads the `.boot2` secti"
               & "on of the object the assembler wrote before linking it: "
               & "a section that is not 256 bytes means the stage and its "
               & "literal pool outgrew the 252 bytes before the checksum, "
               & "and the message gives their size; a relocation in the st"
               & "age, or one elsewhere in the image that refers to it, wo"
               & "uld make the bytes the boot ROM copies and runs at anoth"
               & "er address differ from the ones summed, and the message "
               & "names the relocation and its symbol. Make the stage shor"
               & "ter, or write it with no symbol outside itself and refer"
               & " to it from nowhere.",
            when Catalogue.Image_Block_Object =>
               "The assembled image block is not the IMAGE_DEF block an "
               & "`rp2350-image-block` image carries (D638). refine emits "
               & "the block directly after the vector table and reads the "
               & "`.embedded_block` section of the object the assembler wr"
               & "ote before linking it: the section must be the 20 bytes "
               & "of one block linked to itself, its start and end markers"
               & ", one IMAGE_TYPE item of one word saying an Arm executab"
               & "le for RP2350 that runs in Secure state, and the LAST it"
               & "em giving that word, with no relocation in it. The messa"
               & "ge names the part that is not. refine writes these words"
               & " itself, so this is a defect of refine or of the assembl"
               & "er it ran rather than of the program; report it with the"
               & " message.",
            when Catalogue.ESP_Image_Object =>
               "The linked executable cannot become the ESP application "
               & "image an `esp-app-image` description asks for, or the im"
               & "age refine wrote does not read back as it was made (D685"
               & "). refine writes `OUT.bin` from the linked ELF's loaded "
               & "segments: every one must lie in a region of the descript"
               & "ion, there may be at most 16, and the image's entry must"
               & " be `_landin_firmware_entry`. After writing it refine re"
               & "ads the file again and holds its header, extended header"
               & ", segments, checksum and SHA-256 to the executable; the "
               & "message names the first that is not. A segment outside t"
               & "he description's regions comes from a developer's linker"
               & " script or an object of a developer's own; the read-back"
               & " is a defect of refine or of the host's filesystem, so r"
               & "eport it with the message.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Malformed =>
               "`refine svd` read an SVD that is not XML in the subset i"
               & "t reads (D555). The message says what was met and the li"
               & "ne and column it was met at: bytes that are not UTF-8, a"
               & "n end tag that does not close the element open, an attri"
               & "bute given twice, an entity other than XML's five, a doc"
               & "ument type declaration, or text outside the root element"
               & ". An SVD is a vendor's file, fetched by its hash and nev"
               & "er edited; one that is refused here is not the file its "
               & "policy names, or is truncated. Fetch it again with `scri"
               & "pts/fetch_inputs.py`.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Policy_Invalid =>
               "`refine svd` cannot read its selection policy (D556): th"
               & "e policy is not JSON, not schema 2, lacks a member it ne"
               & "eds, names a member refine does not read, or gives one o"
               & "f the wrong shape, such as a read policy other than `nor"
               & "mal`, `modify` or `refused`, or a mask that is not a `0x"
               & "` 32-bit value. The message names the member. A reviewer"
               & "'s notes belong under `provenance`, which is not read. `"
               & "devices/README.md` describes every member.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Input_Mismatch =>
               "The SVD `refine svd` was given is not the one its policy"
               & " was reviewed against (D556): its SHA-256, its device na"
               & "me or its version differs from the policy's. A policy's "
               & "access policies and corrections were reviewed for one fi"
               & "le, and a different file is not covered by that review. "
               & "Fetch the SVD the policy names, or review the policy aga"
               & "inst the new file and give its hash.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Form_Unsupported =>
               "A selected register of the SVD uses a form `refine svd` "
               & "does not read (D557): an array (`dim`) of peripherals, r"
               & "egisters or fields, a register in a `cluster`, a registe"
               & "r or field derived from another, an `alternateGroup`, a "
               & "derived peripheral that adds registers or is derived fro"
               & "m a derived one, a width other than 32 bits, a default e"
               & "numerated value or one with don't-care bits, or a number"
               & " with a multiplier. The message names the element and th"
               & "e line it is at. Select registers that use the forms D55"
               & "7 lists, or extend the importer."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An enumerated value whose name is not an ASCII letter fo"
               & "llowed by letters, digits and underscores, such as RP204"
               & "0's `1_15MHZ` or `2mA`, cannot be an atom. Every selecte"
               & "d field with one is named in a single refusal, each with"
               & " its first such name; list each in the policy's `numeric"
               & "_enums`, which reads the field as a plain number.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Device_Inconsistent =>
               "The SVD describes a selected register in a way that cann"
               & "ot be generated as it says (D557): two fields overlap, a"
               & " field lies outside its register, an enumerated value do"
               & "es not fit its field or encodes a value twice, a propert"
               & "y the register needs is given nowhere it inherits from, "
               & "an address is not a word-aligned 32-bit address, an alte"
               & "rnate register is at another address, or two vendor name"
               & "s become one Landin name once lowercased and joined. The"
               & " message names the element. Leave the register out of th"
               & "e selection, or record a reviewed correction.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Not_Found =>
               "The policy selects what the SVD does not have (D556): a "
               & "peripheral, a register, or a register's alternate. A reg"
               & "ister that is part of a `dim` array is not found by its "
               & "expanded name, and the message says so when the peripher"
               & "al has arrays. Correct the selection's spelling against "
               & "the SVD.",
            when Catalogue.Svd_Output_Refused =>
               "`refine svd` cannot prepare its output group (D558, D907"
               & "): the output root is missing, a link or not a directory"
               & "; a destination is a directory or link, or aliases a pro"
               & "tected input; a retained publication needs recovery; or "
               & "the manifest names a file outside the output directory. "
               & "Correct the named path or manifest, or choose another `-"
               & "-out-dir`. For a retained `.refine-publication-...` work"
               & "space, inspect its `destination-...` records and recover"
               & " the previous or new output before removing it and retry"
               & "ing. Preparation can already have created private stagin"
               & "g; later publication or cleanup failures are L0005 and c"
               & "an leave recovered or retained versions. Follow those re"
               & "covery messages rather than assuming nothing was written"
               & ".",
            when Catalogue.Bindings_Policy_Invalid =>
               "`refine bindings` cannot read its policy (D820): it is n"
               & "ot UTF-8 JSON, names a key twice, is not schema 1, lacks"
               & " a key it needs or names one refine does not read, gives"
               & " one of the wrong shape, or binds for another ABI than `"
               & "--target` names, a data model or calling convention amon"
               & "g them, which `cortex-m0`'s policy must name (D935). The"
               & " message names the key or the declaration, and for a fun"
               & "ction, callback or incoming entry without `parameters` s"
               & "ays to write `""parameters"": {}` when no parameter is a r"
               & "eference. A policy's every key is described in the [bind"
               & "ing policy reference](../bindings/README.md). With an in"
               & "stalled compiler, run `refine help bindings` for the add"
               & "ress of its generated reading copy.",
            when Catalogue.Bindings_Clang_Refused =>
               "The Clang `refine bindings` was given cannot be used as "
               & "asked (D820): it cannot be run, a root it is given is no"
               & "t a directory, it failed, and the message carries its er"
               & "ror output with the request's paths replaced by names th"
               & "at do not depend on where it ran, or it describes anothe"
               & "r ABI than the target's: another triple, data model, byt"
               & "e order, sign of plain `char` or, on Cortex-M, procedure"
               & " call standard, float unit, enum size or hosted environm"
               & "ent (D935). A header reached through an absolute path un"
               & "der none of the roots the request names is refused too, "
               & "since what is generated could then depend on where it wa"
               & "s. A relative dependency that escapes Clang's retained w"
               & "orkspace, even if it reenters, is also refused: its exte"
               & "rnal directory authority cannot be retained by normalizi"
               & "ng the path. Use an absolute include under a declared ro"
               & "ot, or name the header through `--include-dir`. Name the"
               & " pinned Clang with `--clang`, and every root a header ne"
               & "eds with `--include-dir` or `--system-include-dir`."
               & LF
               & LF
               & "An incompatible child-exit signal policy also refuses Cl"
               & "ang before it starts: use the default `SIGCHLD` disposit"
               & "ion with `SA_NOCLDWAIT` clear, as L0501 explains.",
            when Catalogue.Bindings_Declaration_Refused =>
               "A declaration the policy selects cannot be bound (D820),"
               & " and the message names the policy declaration and the po"
               & "sition: the header no longer has it (a stale policy), a "
               & "reference position has no policy or a scalar one has one"
               & ", which names the key to remove, or the declaration uses"
               & " a form `bindings/README.md` lists as refused, such as a"
               & "n extended floating type, a calling convention attribute"
               & ", an anonymous aggregate or a wrapper that would forward"
               & " a C variadic tail, or, on freestanding `cortex-m0`, a n"
               & "ullable callback or a `_Thread_local` object, whose adap"
               & "ters need a C library (D938). A Landin name two declarat"
               & "ions would share is refused here too. Correct the policy"
               & ", or select another declaration.",
            when Catalogue.Bindings_Output_Refused =>
               "`refine bindings` cannot prepare its output group (D820,"
               & " D907): the output root is a symbolic link or not a dire"
               & "ctory, an output is a directory or link, an output alias"
               & "es a protected header, policy, response file or selected"
               & " tool, or an earlier publication needs recovery. Correct"
               & " the named path or choose another `--out-dir`. Keep a na"
               & "med `.refine-publication-...` workspace until its `desti"
               & "nation-...` records and retained previous or new outputs"
               & " have been inspected and recovered; remove it only after"
               & " recovery. Preparation can already have created private "
               & "staging. A later publication or cleanup failure is L0005"
               & " and can leave outputs installed or recovery entries ret"
               & "ained, as that diagnostic reports.",
            when Catalogue.Firmware_Foreign_Section =>
               "A firmware image linked with C archives, through `linker"
               & ".library` with `linker.directory` or `-L DIR`, holds som"
               & "ething compiler-owned startup cannot honour (D923, D924)"
               & ". Reset copies data, clears BSS and calls the firmware e"
               & "ntry; it runs no C constructor, has one thread and no th"
               & "read pointer, and loads nothing at run time. So the imag"
               & "e is refused, and removed, when an archive brought C con"
               & "structors, an `.init_array`, `.preinit_array` or `.ctors"
               & "` section that the derived script keeps so that it canno"
               & "t be dropped unseen; thread-local storage, a `.tdata` or"
               & " `.tbss` section from a `_Thread_local` or `__thread` va"
               & "riable; or a dynamic linkage, which a shared object woul"
               & "d bring. The message names the section. Build the librar"
               & "y without constructors and call its initialisation from "
               & "the firmware entry; declare a thread-local variable as o"
               & "rdinary static data; and link the library's static archi"
               & "ve built for the firmware's core.");

